2026-02-10 02:04:30,593 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document Understanding the Mechanics of American Options

American options outline the timeframe when the option holder can exercise their option contract rights. These rights allow the holder to buy or sell—depending on if the option is a call or put—the underlying asset, at the set strike price on or before the predetermined expiration date. American-style options are more valuable than European options because investors can exercise them anytime before they expire. However, exercising early comes with an extra cost or premium.

Generally, the last day to exercise a weekly American option is Friday of its expiration week. For monthly American options, the last exercise day is typically the third Friday of the month.

The majority of exchange-traded options on single stocks are American, while options on indexes tend to be European style. is relevant
