2026-02-10 02:05:41,165 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document What Is a European Option?

A European option is a financial contract that can only be exercised on its expiration date. This is in contrast to an American option, which allows the holder to exercise it at any time before it expires. Most index options are European, which means they can't be exercised early. The Black-Scholes model is commonly used to value European options and assess their fair price. is relevant
